## Git Version
**Syntax:**
```bash
$ git --version

Example:
git version 2.55.0.windows.5

## Git Clone
**Purpose:** Clone a remote repository to the local machine.

Steps
Open the repository on GitHub.
Click Code.
Select HTTPS.
Copy the repository URL.
Run the git clone command in Git Bash.

**Syntax:**
```bash
git clone <repository-URL>

Example:
git clone https://github.com/gopika/git-jou.git

This creates a local copy of the git-jou repository on your computer.


